KG42.register("clusters-3c9a992a71d27fa96c4cbf70",{"id":"10-hierarchical_coordination::v142-d-K002","paper":"10-hierarchical_coordination","label":"Bilateral Matching, Allocation, and Pairwise Pricing under Strategy One","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K002","label":"Bilateral Matching, Allocation, and Pairwise Pricing under Strategy One","market_meaning":"After receiving bids, the LMO determines matching and energy allocation according to the Strategy One objective and existing bilateral constraints, and determines independent bilateral prices for matched transactions. Duplicated mathematical content in the matching, clearing, and participation chains is retained as different representations of the same decision; bid price indices, pairwise pricing inputs, and aggregate quantity constraints across counterparties still require clarification.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01","v141-a-M02"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["bidding","coordination","clearing","matching","participation","pricing"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"The core decision is restricted to Strategy One in M02; the general matching and price independence in M01 provide background, the bidding chains provide submitted inputs, and R008 and R010 retain the case time point conditions. The general description does not extend the scope of applicability of the Strategy One objective, and mutual exclusivity of case submissions is not automatically equated with mutual exclusivity of bilateral transactions.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"With submitted bids as inputs and the quantities and prices of matched transactions as outputs, this brings together LMO allocation, counterparty selection, bilateral role constraints, and pricing. Local duplications in R009, R011, and R012 are not counted as additional independent rules; how prosumers optimize bids remains primarily assigned to K001.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R004","ownership":"primary","role":"context","rationale":"Preserves the primary assignment of the general P2P matching procedure as a higher-level description of Strategy One; its general scope can still be referenced jointly by Strategy Two."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R006","ownership":"primary","role":"support","rationale":"Preserves the general statement of transaction price independence, which is given concrete form by the Strategy One pricing chain, without counting it as an additional independent pricing mechanism."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R009","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Represents the Strategy One objective, feasibility constraints, bilateral allocation, and definition of net transaction quantity."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R011","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Represents the bid inputs and counterparty matching meaning of the same allocation decision; its duplicated block constraints and objective are not counted as additional optimization rules."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R012","ownership":"primary","role":"alternative","rationale":"Restates the bilateral direction restrictions in R009 from the participation perspective, retaining the explicit binary definition without counting the rule twice."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R013","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Represents bilateral price calculation after matching and transaction price independence."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R001","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"References only the demand bid blocks already formulated as clearing inputs; their primary assignment remains in K001."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R002","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"References supply quantities and prices already formulated as clearing inputs, retaining the distinction between their roles as prosumer decision variables and LMO parameters."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R008","ownership":"shared","role":"support","rationale":"References the single submission role in the case for comparison with bilateral allocation constraints, without inferring that the two have been established as mathematically equivalent."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R010","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"Provides the input procedure in the case for submitting the corresponding curves to the LMO."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-L01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R010","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R009","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C001","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C004","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C005"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e34"],"rationale":"The original case text explicitly states that transaction quantities are calculated from submitted curves after their receipt, linking the input procedure to the entry point of the Strategy One calculation; this assembly relationship does not add a scientific graph edge."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-L02","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R009","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C007"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e34","v141-b-g02-e16"],"rationale":"The buying and selling roles at time points in the submission layer and the directions of counterparty pairs in the allocation layer constrain inputs and outputs, respectively; their applicable granularities differ, so they are referenced only as complementary elements."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-L03","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R009","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x2"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R009::theta::v141-c-R009-T-B"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e12","v141-b-g02-e18"],"rationale":"The submitted demand block quantity defined in M01 becomes an upper-bound input for clearing in M02; this transfer does not involve the unspecified conversion between ω and m."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-L04","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R009","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-X003","v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-X004"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R009::theta::v141-c-R009-T-O","v141-c-R009::theta::v141-c-R009-T-LAM-O"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e12","v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g02-e20"],"rationale":"The source explicitly treats supply block quantities and prices as submission outputs and as quantity upper bounds and objective inputs for the LMO; both the original mechanism and the local variable roles are retained."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-L05","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R009","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R011","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R009::x::v141-c-R009-X-P2P-SEL-BL","v141-c-R009::x::v141-c-R009-X-P2P-BUY-BL","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C006"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R011::x::v141-c-R011-x1","v141-c-R011::x::v141-c-R011-x2","v141-c-R011::phi::v141-c-R011-C006"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g02-e20","v141-b-g02-e21"],"rationale":"The same Strategy One problem implements matching through bilateral block allocation; R009 represents the complete extracted constraint family, while R011 provides the counterparty and bid input perspective."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-L06","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R012","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R009","kind":"alternative_representation","from_refs":["v141-c-R012::phi::v141-c-R012-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C007"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e16"],"rationale":"The two chains express the same bilateral direction and capacity restrictions under Strategy One, with R012 explicitly listing the binary domain in its expression; both representations are preserved and are not counted as additional independent restrictions."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-L07","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R011","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R013","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R011::V::matching.counterparties","v141-c-R011::phi::v141-c-R011-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R013::phi::v141-c-R013-C001","v141-c-R013::phi::v141-c-R013-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e24"],"rationale":"The original text makes the two parties being matched a condition for the applicability of pairwise pricing; only the decision result and pricing scope are linked here, without supplying the missing rule for selecting block prices."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-L08","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R011","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R011::phi::v141-c-R011-C001","v141-c-R011::phi::v141-c-R011-C002","v141-c-R011::phi::v141-c-R011-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g02-e20","v141-b-g02-e21"],"rationale":"The general matching procedure in M01 is implemented concretely by Strategy One in M02; the general background itself does not establish any new optimization dependency."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-L09","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R013","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R013::phi::v141-c-R013-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g02-e02"],"rationale":"General transaction price independence is restated within the scope of Strategy One; the two objects with different scopes are retained, without inferring that traded quantities are also mutually independent."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-O01","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R004::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R008::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R009::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R010::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R011::V::bidding.demand"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g02-e12","v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g02-e20","v141-b-g02-e34"],"rationale":"The same demand submission function appears in bidding, receipt, and clearing input positions; the mechanisms and case conditions are retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-O02","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::V::bidding.supply","v141-c-R004::V::bidding.supply","v141-c-R008::V::bidding.supply","v141-c-R009::V::bidding.supply","v141-c-R010::V::bidding.supply","v141-c-R011::V::bidding.supply"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g02-e12","v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g02-e20","v141-b-g02-e34"],"rationale":"The same supply submission function extends through bidding and clearing inputs, without merging associated edges under different conditions."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-O03","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R009::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R010::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R011::V::coordination.local_operator"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g02-e20","v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e34"],"rationale":"All are LMO functions for receiving bids and coordinating transactions; sharing a node does not imply that the respective decision scopes are identical."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-O04","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::V::matching.counterparties","v141-c-R011::V::matching.counterparties","v141-c-R013::V::matching.counterparties"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g02-e20","v141-b-g02-e24"],"rationale":"General matching, Strategy One matching, and the matching condition used for pricing reference the same existing functional node, with their respective scopes retained separately."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-O05","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R006::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R013::V::pricing.local"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g02-e02","v141-b-g02-e24"],"rationale":"The two chains use the existing node to represent bilateral transaction pricing; the node is not interpreted as a uniform transaction price for the entire region."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-O06","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-X003","v141-c-R009::theta::v141-c-R009-T-O","v141-c-R011::theta::v141-c-R011-t1"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e12","v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g02-e20"],"rationale":"The same submitted supply block quantity changes from a prosumer output to a fixed input for Strategy One; all differences in the local roles and units of x and theta are retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-O07","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x2","v141-c-R009::theta::v141-c-R009-T-B","v141-c-R011::theta::v141-c-R011-t2"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e12","v141-b-g02-e18"],"rationale":"The submitted demand block with the same j, t, m indices serves as an input upper bound in clearing and matching; its distinct roles as a decision output and a fixed parameter are maintained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-O08","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-X004","v141-c-R009::theta::v141-c-R009-T-LAM-O","v141-c-R011::theta::v141-c-R011-t3"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e12","v141-b-g02-e20"],"rationale":"The supply block offer price is passed from the prosumer decision output into the Strategy One objective; it is not merged with the forecast LEM price or pairwise price inputs without an m index."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-O09","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R009::theta::v141-c-R009-T-LAM-B","v141-c-R011::theta::v141-c-R011-t4"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e20"],"rationale":"Both objects retain the demand price indexed by i as printed in Eq. (24); its relationship to other prices indexed by j remains unresolved."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-O10","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R009::x::v141-c-R009-X-P2P-SEL-BL","v141-c-R011::x::v141-c-R011-x1"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g02-e20"],"rationale":"The electricity sale allocation quantity under the same Strategy One and with the same bilateral and bid block indices is used in the clearing and matching representations, respectively."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-O11","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R009::x::v141-c-R009-X-P2P-BUY-BL","v141-c-R011::x::v141-c-R011-x2"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g02-e20"],"rationale":"The same bilateral electricity purchase block allocation quantity under Strategy One; the original unit annotations and local functional bindings are maintained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-O12","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R009::x::v141-c-R009-X-P2P-SEL","v141-c-R012::x::v141-c-R012-x-P2p-plus"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e16"],"rationale":"Both objects are the total electricity sale quantity for the same ordered trading pair under Strategy One and are not merged with the decision result under Strategy Two that uses the same symbol."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-O13","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R009::x::v141-c-R009-X-P2P-BUY","v141-c-R012::x::v141-c-R012-x-P2p-minus"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e16"],"rationale":"The total electricity purchase quantity for the same ordered trading pair under Strategy One serves different local roles in clearing and participation constraints."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-O14","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R009::x::v141-c-R009-X-U","v141-c-R012::x::v141-c-R012-x-u"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e16"],"rationale":"The same bilateral buying and selling state under Strategy One; it is not equated with a prosumer's state within a scenario or a uniform submission role for the entire time point."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-O15","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R009::theta::v141-c-R009-T-PBAR","v141-c-R012::theta::v141-c-R012-theta-Pbar"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e16"],"rationale":"A repeated declaration of the same capacity upper-bound parameter under Strategy One, with the original unit differences retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-O16","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R009::theta::v141-c-R009-T-LBAR","v141-c-R012::theta::v141-c-R012-theta-Lbar"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e16"],"rationale":"A repeated declaration of the same maximum consumption parameter under Strategy One, with the original objects remaining independently accessible."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-O17","kind":"same_expression","member_refs":["v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C002","v141-c-R011::phi::v141-c-R011-C005"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C002","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e18"],"rationale":"Both objects express Eq. (20) within the same Strategy One scope, with R009 selected only as the display representative; the original constraints in both chains and the differences between their limits and links edges remain unchanged."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-O18","kind":"same_expression","member_refs":["v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C003","v141-c-R011::phi::v141-c-R011-C004"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C003","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e18"],"rationale":"Both objects express Eq. (21) with the same scope of applicability; selecting a representative is only for display and does not delete constraints or merge their graph edges."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-O19","kind":"alternative_representation","member_refs":["v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C007","v141-c-R012::phi::v141-c-R012-C001"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e16"],"rationale":"Both represent Eqs. (17), (18), but the R012 expression explicitly includes the binary domain, whereas R009 provides it through the variable definition; this representational difference is retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-O20","kind":"alternative_representation","member_refs":["v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C006","v141-c-R011::phi::v141-c-R011-C006"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e20","v141-b-g02-e21"],"rationale":"The two objects represent the same Strategy One objective; R009 also explicitly includes minimization and a reference to the feasible set, while the R011 expression provides only the objective definition. The complete objects are not judged to be exact duplicates, nor are they counted as a second optimization."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G01","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"The demand price in Eq. (24) uses the i index, whereas the electricity purchase block multiplied by it and that block's upper bound use the buyer index j; the surrounding definitions also differ in their use of j and i. R009 and R011 retain the same printed form, but this does not confirm the economic meaning or establish a link to the price indexed by j in R001.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R009","v141-c-R011"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x3","v141-c-R009::theta::v141-c-R009-T-LAM-B","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C006","v141-c-R011::theta::v141-c-R011-t4"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e12","v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g02-e20"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the original equation and the participant to whom the price corresponds, obtaining an explanation from the authors if necessary; retain the existing expression without independently changing the index or claiming equivalence to social welfare."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G02","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The supply and demand prices in Eq. (26) have no m index, whereas the clearing objective uses bid block prices; when multiple blocks are traded, how the inputs to the pairwise price are selected or aggregated is not specified. Block price parameters cannot be directly mapped to the parameters without block indices in R013.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R009","v141-c-R011","v141-c-R013"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R009::theta::v141-c-R009-T-LAM-O","v141-c-R009::theta::v141-c-R009-T-LAM-B","v141-c-R013::theta::theta_lambda_o_jt","v141-c-R013::theta::theta_lambda_b_it","v141-c-R013::phi::v141-c-R013-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e20","v141-b-g02-e24"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Verify the correspondence between matched transactions and bid blocks and the rules for pricing inputs; after completing the upstream interface, assess whether quantities and prices form a complete, executable result."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G03","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The upper bounds in Eqs. (17) to (21) are imposed separately on each trading pair, and the existing expressions contain no restriction on cumulative use of the same bid block or participant capacity across counterparties; bilateral states are also not bound to a uniform buying or selling role at a time point. These constraints do not support an inference that the total bid quantity will not be allocated repeatedly among multiple counterparties, or that transaction direction is already uniform across the entire time point.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R008","v141-c-R009","v141-c-R011","v141-c-R012","v141-c-R010"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C002","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C003","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C007","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C009","v141-c-R012::x::v141-c-R012-x-u"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e16","v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g02-e19","v141-b-g02-e34","v141-b-g02-e36"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Verify the meaning of bid block capacity, the treatment of remaining quantities across counterparties, and whether role consistency is guaranteed by unextracted conditions or algorithms; in the absence of a source, retain the gap and do not introduce aggregate quantity constraints."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G04","category":"ontology_extension","description":"The existing pricing.local represents independent bilateral transaction prices and cannot be interpreted as a uniform regional price. The related proposal v141-b-g01-prop-p2p-price remains unapproved.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R006","v141-c-R013"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R006::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R013::V::pricing.local"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g02-e02","v141-b-g02-e24"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g01-prop-p2p-price"],"required_work":"Manually inspect the interpretation of the existing node in this paper and whether an ontology extension is needed; this round retains only the bilateral scope and does not insert new nodes."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G05","category":"unverified_source","description":"Neither the sources of this cluster nor the existing mathematical content in C has undergone an independent source audit or C2 review in this experiment; mappings of the same quantity and duplicated expressions do not validate units, indices, or scientific correctness.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R004","v141-c-R006","v141-c-R008","v141-c-R009","v141-c-R010","v141-c-R011","v141-c-R012","v141-c-R013"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g02-e12","v141-b-g02-e16","v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g02-e19","v141-b-g02-e20","v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e24","v141-b-g02-e34"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually inspect all chains and mappings, and independently check formulas, units, applicability conditions, and citations; eligibility as candidate evidence must not be treated as scientific approval."}]},"rule_refs":["10-hierarchical_coordination::v141-c-R004","10-hierarchical_coordination::v141-c-R006","10-hierarchical_coordination::v141-c-R009","10-hierarchical_coordination::v141-c-R011","10-hierarchical_coordination::v141-c-R012","10-hierarchical_coordination::v141-c-R013","10-hierarchical_coordination::v141-c-R001","10-hierarchical_coordination::v141-c-R002","10-hierarchical_coordination::v141-c-R008","10-hierarchical_coordination::v141-c-R010"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-4fd16cbd90d234cb","COMP-559b64eb7df63aa5","COMP-b3f649e90c1f17b9","COMP-b9841ac99d9d29b8","COMP-be69d81055b11c0c","COMP-da34359f040da554","KG31-0645fab4a79eb10b","KG31-71938ef56b613c45"]});
